{
  "$schema": "../gen/schemas/desktop-schema.json",
  "identifier": "default",
  "description": "Capability for the main Blue Environment window \u2014 grants access to all custom Rust commands and required core plugin permissions. NOTE: this file previously had a duplicate, malformed override \u2014 `{\"identifier\": \"core:default\", \"allow\": []}` (empty allow list) sitting right after the plain \"core:default\" string that grants the real default set, plus a matching duplicate for \"http:default\". Confirmed as the actual root cause of an app-wide breakage (terminal PTY denied, Files/System Monitor/app launcher all failing) \u2014 not a hypothetical risk, a real one reproduced and then fixed by removing both duplicate entries. If IPC/commands break again app-wide (not just for a specific webview), check this file first for a duplicate identifier with a narrower \"allow\" list shadowing the real grant, before assuming a webview-scoping issue. Also now includes an explicit allow-<command> permission for every one of this app's ~257 custom commands (see build.rs's own comment for why -- a belt-and-suspenders fix for real, reproduced 'not allowed by ACL' errors on multiple unrelated custom commands, despite Tauri's documented default that should have made this unnecessary). Mechanically generated from main.rs's generate_handler! list -- if commands are added/removed there, re-run the same extraction against this file and build.rs together, don't hand-edit just one of the two.",
